{"The expectations in `test_thread_queue_parallel_error_handling` contradict the test docstring - docstring states errors should not block commits but assertion enforces the opposite, and since worker marks offsets complete in `finally` block, offsets become committable even when processing raises": 0.8725232481956482, "The worker loop relies on non-existent `queue.ShutDown` exception and `Queue.shutdown` method, which will prevent clean shutdown and may hang threads - `queue.Queue` has neither, so `work_queue.get()` will block indefinitely and `FixedQueuePool.shutdown` will raise `AttributeError`": 0.9475576877593994, "`join` ignores the `timeout` parameter and re-invokes `close`, which means callers can't bound the wait time and a second `join()` will redundantly re-run shutdown logic - `close()` should initiate shutdown and `join(timeout=...)` should only wait for in-flight work": 0.8725398182868958, "The queue worker and pool use `queue.ShutDown` and `q.shutdown(...)`, but the standard library `queue.Queue` class does not define this exception or method - this will raise attribute/exception errors at runtime": 0.8817964196205139, "`FixedQueuePool.shutdown()` is called from both `SimpleQueueProcessingStrategy.close/terminate` and `ResultsStrategyFactory.shutdown`, which can lead to double-shutdown of the same workers/queues - consider making ownership explicit or making `shutdown()` safely idempotent with guards": 0.825507640838623}